what the hell is time fall when you  first boot up death stranding you may  ask yourself this very question among  many many others however time fall and  weather play a huge role in death  stranding story and gameplay if you  aren't careful one bad time fall storm  can ruin an otherwise flawless delivery  here's a quick explainer on how to  survive death strandings weather system  and time fall time fall is basically  rain if rain eroded in deteriorated  objects at a much quicker pace anything  the time fall rain touches other than  raincoats for some reason will degrade  over time this applies to packages you  are carrying vehicles left out in the  rain equipment attached to your suit and  structures placed in the world early on  the best way to avoid time fall is to  find shelter in the form of caves  outposts and cities and wait out the  storm  when you rest in a safe house or private  room you will automatically pass time by  30 minutes unfortunately if you plan to  weather the storm outside you have to  wait in real-time most of the time this  is less than ideal especially if you are  doing a time delivery however there are  moments when time fall is unavoidable  one thing to consider in these scenarios  is how to load up your cargo packages  and boxes attached to the suit or  stacked above your backpack are more  exposed to time fall should there be a  storm on your journey a good rule of  thumb is to put important packages deep  in your backpack that way time fall  can't get to them as easily if you  notice that one of your containers is in  bad shape you can always repair it with  container repair spray this will fix up  the container but not its contents if  the cargo itself has been damaged  there's no way to repair it fortunately  during chapter 3 Sam will gain access to  some new tech that will make his life a  lot easier first is a weather forecast  built into his cuff links if you open  the map and click r3 twice you can see  the forecast for the next 30 minutes  once you've unlocked this avoiding time  fall storms becomes much easier in  Episode three you will also unlock a  time fall shelter using an upgraded PCC  you can create a giant umbrella that  protects Sam and his vehicle from  precipitation and even sprays out  container repair spray while you're  there better yet you can also advance  time by 10 minutes if you find yourself  in a storm that should end soon you can  always craft a time fall shelter and  wait it out keep in mind though that  some storms can last  very long time and the more you advance  time the sooner your other constructions  will deteriorate near the end of episode  3 there's also a character that gives  Sam a rain cover for his backpack that  will give your cargo an extra layer of  protection cargo degradation isn't the  only thing to worry about during a storm  when the rain turns black it means that  BTS are about to pay you a visit in most  cases especially early on the best thing  to do is to sneak by them this does mean  that your cargo will be exposed to rain  longer but that's better than it getting  scattered everywhere or worse destroyed  another good way to minimize your time  exposed to time fall is to use vehicles  trucks may not be able to protect your  cargo from reckless driving but they  will protect it from rain meanwhile  bikes may not offer as much protection  but you can speed right through storms  however if you try to speed through  black rain if BTS will stop you in your  tracks keep in mind that vehicles like  everything else deteriorate over time  due to time falls the last thing you  want is for your truck to break down in  the middle of nowhere with tons of cargo  in the back make sure to leave your  vehicles in a garage every now and then  to repair them and save often rain and  time fall isn't the only thing you  should look out for occasionally you and  Sam will have to contend with wind wind  is far less dangerous than rain but it  can drain your stamina quicker and make  it harder for Sam to find his footing  when his cargo is stacked high however  there is a more dangerous form of time  fall which takes the form of snow along  with forcing you to move slower it  degrades cargo even quicker  I'd recommend avoiding the snow as much  as possible until you have better  equipment to deal with it this is just a  basic rundown of how weather works in  death stranding and how you can prepare  for it keep in mind that this guide only  covers episodes 1 through 3 and some  more useful strategies will come into  play later in the game thanks for  watching and stay tuned to game spot for  more on deaths stranding  [Music]
 

